        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mark Steven Johnson, Robert Thornby, Priscilla Dean, John Irving\n- Films: Simon Birch, West of Broadway\n- Roles: screenwriter, film director, producer, director, actor\n- Topics: silent era, lost films\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Thornby was born on March 27, 1888, and he was an American director and actor of the silent era.\n- West of Broadway is a lost 1926 American silent romantic comedy/Western film directed by Robert Thornby and starring Priscilla Dean.\n- Mark Steven Johnson was born on October 30, 1964, and he is an American screenwriter, film director, and producer.\n- Simon Birch is a 1998 American comedy-drama film loosely based on A Prayer for Owen Meany by John Irving, and Mark Steven Johnson directed and wrote the screenplay for it.\n- Robert Thornby died on March 6, 1953.",
